==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|fi|gmq-osw|frēadagher|frē(i)adagher, frīadagher}}, from {{der|fi|gmw-pro|*Frījā dag}}.

Since Finnish historically lacks ''f'' and initial consonant clusters (such as ''fr''), the word was adapted to fit the language's phonological rules. These changes can be imagined as *''freja'' => *''pereja'' => *''perja'' (On the first step, F turns to P, and an epenthetic vowel appears to avoid the cluster [PR]. Then, on the second step, the unstressed vowel is dropped). For the -''antai'' ending, compare {{m|fi|maanantai|t=Monday}} and {{m|fi|sunnuntai|t=Sunday}}.

